{"labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le16ob11re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "If you remember the time before mobile phones were invented, you know that people had no choice but to interact. This is no longer. If you should happen to be with a group of people, look around. Someone will be thumbing through their e-mails. Another will be having their attention drawn to a news item or Twitter feed. Someone else will be checking in with other friends. No one will be talking to each other.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le16ob11re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "This is killing conversation. If you were to try to converse, what would happen? Would they just nod and continue? Probably.  You'll be considered naive if you don't agree. We will be growing more and more accustomed to sharing physical space without sharing our experience. By the time they are adults most children will have carried phones with them for years.\n<br>\nThey will have been living in their heads focused on their screens for a long time. If you were to take their phones away, they would have a hard time adjusting to the novel face-to-face concept.", "id": 2, "time": "24000", "image": "engenn10le16ob11re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "When phones were first invented people were both excited and appalled. The idea of someone disrupting a family dinner was unsettling. Then phones were walked into our workplace and leisure area. Payphones sprung up on sidewalks. Answering machines recorded the messages of those we missed. Now we have been given a device that is with us waking and sleeping. We are never unplugged. <br/>\nIn the future we will have moved into even more connectivity. We will be living organisms enmeshed with the World Wide Web. We will have become part of the machine, like it or not.", "id": 3, "time": "59000", "image": "engenn10le16ob11re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le16ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le16ob11re2img02.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about technology and personal dilemmas.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about likely or unlikely situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How often are you distracted by your phone when you are out with other people?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How do you think social interaction changes when people have their cell phones out?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " When should cell phones be off or at least out of sight?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 